@keycloak = http://localhost:8180/realms/ecommerce/protocol/openid-connect/token

### Alice (customer)
# @name alice
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=ecommerce-cli&username=alice&password=alice

### Bob (customer)
# @name bob
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=ecommerce-cli&username=bob&password=bob

### Shop admin
# @name shopAdmin
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=ecommerce-cli&username=shop-admin&password=shop-admin

### Alice's profile (created automatically on this first call)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/customers/me
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.access_token}}

### Alice tries the admin API → 403
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/admin/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Hack", "slug": "hack" }

### No token → 401
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/cart